Why doesn't being hit by a missile attack stop the current occupation?
It's a bit annoying to get killed by arrows while trying to force a lock,
and it doesn't seem reasonable that being pumped full of arrows should
be somehow less noteworthy than being hit by a swung weapon.

Second topic:  it seems like armor class is trying to code too much
information in one number.  Dragons have a good armor class because
they have a tough hide.  Killer bees have a good armor class because
they are small, and thus hard to hit.  Now, if I were attacking killer
bees in real life, I would not use a long sword or even a blessed
katana--I'd swat 'em with my shield, or a rolled up scroll.  But that 
doesn't work in NetHack--a shield has no plus to hit small creatures, 
and you can't just give a shield a global plus because then it would 
hit dragons and ghosts too (I guess), which surely isn't right, is it?  
(I haven't looked all that carefully at the source, so I could totally 
hosed somewhere.)

I like the idea of a "flyswatter" weapon--tourists would surely start
out with one.  Or maybe a "scroll of New York Times", for bashing bees.
"Array Terminator" sounds like a cool weapon too--to bad I'll never find
one :-).

